    "text": "The People’s Republic of China National Day, Oct. 1, marks the day when former Chinese Communist Party head Mao Zedong declared communist control in China. NTD discussed the Chinese Communist Party’s decades of oppression with Trevor Loudon, an author, filmmaker, and public speaker. For more than 30 years, he has researched Marxist movements, as well as the influence of the Chinese Communist Party.\nTrevor Loudon: 76 Years Under CCP Rule Is an Embarrassment for China\nThe People’s Republic of China National Day, Oct. 1, marks the day when former Chinese Communist Party head Mao Zedong declared communist control in China.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 10/1/2025, 11:17:25 PM EDT",
